<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lake Poyang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1363">1363</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-turban-rebellion">Red Turban Rebellion</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-poyang">Lake Poyang</a> was a naval battle fought on Lake Poyang in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> from August to October 1363 between the fleets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-youliang">Chen Youliang</a>, rival leaders of the rebellions against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>. Chen's larger fleet of tower ships had been besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanchang">Nanchang</a>; Zhu's forces used fire-ships against it, and Chen was killed by an arrow. The victory made Zhu, the future Hongwu Emperor, master of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div>
